## Context

Filed at the 0252-family roar (2026-07-13), per the standing-regression-test
rule: the weak worktree predicate had class shape — `[ -f .git ]` appeared in
erg-pr-merge (fixed, 0301) and survives in two sibling guards (0308). A green
per-PR gate does not stop the class from re-entering in an unrelated future
script; only a standing adherence test does.

## Actions

1. Adherence-tier test (tests/, @pytest.mark.adherence style used by this
   repo's bash-suite checks) that greps scripts/ and skills/ for weak
   worktree predicates (`[ -f .git ]` and close variants) outside an
   explicit allowlist.
2. Seed the allowlist with the two 0308 scripts (shrink when 0308 lands)
   and the explanatory comment in skills/merge/erg-pr-merge:26.
3. Prove RED by temporarily adding a weak predicate to a scratch script.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Ratchet test merged, RED-proven, allowlist documented
- [ ] Allowlist shrinks with 0308 (cross-reference both tickets)
- [ ] `make check` passes
